@startuml
!pragma layout smetana

title Trade lifecycle

skinparam state {
    BackgroundColor #D6E8FA
    BorderColor #4A78A8
    FontColor #1A1A1E
    AttributeFontColor #3A3A3E
    ArrowColor #4A78A8
    ArrowFontColor #1A1A1E
    StartColor #4A78A8
    EndColor #4A78A8
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FBF3D3
    BorderColor #C9A227
    FontColor #1A1A1E
}
skinparam BackgroundColor white
skinparam DefaultFontColor #1A1A1E

state "live" as Live {
  state "unauthorised" as Unauthorised #F0E2D0 ##[bold]A87A4A
  state "authorised" as Authorised #F0E2D0 ##[bold]A87A4A

  Unauthorised : Exists; contributes to nothing
  Authorised : Contributes to risk and P&L

  [*] --> Unauthorised
  Unauthorised --> Authorised : Authorise
  Authorised --> Unauthorised : Un-authorise
  Authorised --> Unauthorised : Amend
  Unauthorised --> Unauthorised : Amend
}

state "expired" as Expired
state "cancelled" as Cancelled

Expired : Contract ceased naturally
Cancelled : Removed from the book

[*] --> Live : New
Live --> Expired : Expiry
Live --> Cancelled : Cancellation
Expired --> Live : Unexpire
Cancelled --> Live : Uncancel
Expired --> Expired : Amend
Cancelled --> Cancelled : Amend
Expired --> [*]
Cancelled --> [*]

note right of Live
  Amending an authorised trade returns
  it to unauthorised: the terms Ops
  released are no longer the terms on
  the book, so the decision must be
  taken again. Amending an unauthorised
  one changes nothing but the version.
end note

note bottom of Cancelled
  The substates of live are shown to
  place them, not to model them. They
  are not states of this machine: the
  trade carries an operational
  authorisation flag, whose own
  lifecycle has four values, and
  contribution follows from combining
  the two.
end note

note left of Expired
  Expiry and cancellation are
  reversible. Unexpire and uncancel
  correct a record rather than revive
  an agreement, so a trade returning
  to live arrives unauthorised.
end note

@enduml
